WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:18.451
Got up fast to catch the sunrise.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:35.368
Turns out, everyone camping in the front-row ocean-view spots was still asleep.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.145
The sun came out from above the clouds.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:55.588
I got to see the Xuhai sunrise. Totally satisfied.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:01:01.461
Even though, with all the clouds, it didn't rise straight out of the sea.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:25.118
Looks like the weather should be nice today.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.025
Probably cyclists here for the sunrise too.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:41.001
Or maybe anglers out fishing.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:26.146
A campground cat with real personality.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:45.899
Pretty solid food today.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:20.767
Time for breakfast. Today's route is even tougher.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:47.927
Today's ride is going to be brutal.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:58.805
Starting from the MANA campground.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:05.645
I'm taking the Shouka shortcut.

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:10.817
Entering from the shortcut trailhead.

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:17.624
There will be a fork in the road halfway through.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:22.629
I named it the “Mystery Nakamoto” and pinned it on the map.

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:29.569
Take the wrong turn, and you'll end up at Xuhai Grassland.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:36.109
Take the right one, and you'll reach the Shouka shortcut exit.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:43.249
After that, it's paved road, a gentle climb, and a sweet ride to Shouka.

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:47.020
Life achievement unlocked on the bike!

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:52.025
⚠ Important: today you must bring enough snacks and water.

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:55.929
There are no supply stops.

00:04:55.929 --> 00:05:00.934
Final destination tonight: Shangwu Tianhou Temple.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.669
Mission complete.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:07.674
The highest point on Taiwan's round-island highway!

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:34.334
Xuhai local bread.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:41.875
There are no convenience stores around Xuhai.

00:05:44.044 --> 00:05:49.049
A simple, down-to-earth little community.

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:34.394
The chain is rusty.

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:02.822
The sun is up, and the temperature keeps climbing. It's getting hot.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:24.177
The campground owner lent me some WD-40. Even better.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:40.827
That weird noise is gone.

00:08:01.381 --> 00:08:06.386
The weather today is amazing.

00:08:18.898 --> 00:08:23.903
Test-pushing the bike before and after packing, to avoid a loading disaster.

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:31.711
Okay. 👌

00:08:46.493 --> 00:08:51.498
Saying goodbye to the campsite.

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:57.671
Heading out for the next destination.

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:48.521
This is an industrial road.

00:09:48.521 --> 00:09:53.526
Google Maps will route you this way.

00:09:53.526 --> 00:09:58.531
But there's no GPS signal in the middle, so be careful.

00:09:59.366 --> 00:10:04.371
It's mainly used to reach Xuhai Grassland.

00:10:07.674 --> 00:10:12.679
It's too steep. With the sun hood on, I can barely breathe.

00:11:43.903 --> 00:11:48.908
Only insects and birds. It's so quiet you can hear cars from far away.

00:11:59.085 --> 00:12:03.623
One big road, one small road. Which one should I take?

00:12:08.028 --> 00:12:13.033
Let's gamble on the big road.

00:12:48.368 --> 00:12:53.373
Emergency snacks I stocked up at the 7-Eleven in Manzhou yesterday.

00:12:56.042 --> 00:13:01.047
I've got a bad feeling. I might end up eating lunch on the mountain.

00:13:04.751 --> 00:13:09.756
There's nobody around.

00:13:19.032 --> 00:13:24.037
I'm practically crawling while pushing the bike.

00:13:51.164 --> 00:13:56.169
Not good. This is the end of the big road.

00:14:09.416 --> 00:14:14.421
I feel like this lady runs into lost travelers every single day.

00:14:28.935 --> 00:14:33.940
⚠ The lady kindly warned me about the dangerous downhill.

00:14:39.546 --> 00:14:44.551
She was super nice and reminded me again and again.

00:14:57.664 --> 00:15:02.669
An 8.63% grade. Braking all the way down.

00:15:04.537 --> 00:15:09.542
Am I going to be able to stop?

00:15:12.479 --> 00:15:17.484
The sound is so sharp even I can't stand it.

00:15:18.718 --> 00:15:23.723
Are my disc brakes going to fall apart?

00:15:27.293 --> 00:15:32.298
This is wild. The steepest downhill I've ever ridden.

00:15:33.733 --> 00:15:38.738
⚠ I need to watch my brakes—and my jaw.

00:15:44.477 --> 00:15:52.285
If I crash here, I'll probably roll all the way to the “Mystery Nakamoto.”

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:12.305
It's shaking so much that getting off and pushing is safer.

00:16:21.648 --> 00:16:26.653
So the Mystery Nakamoto actually means the way to Shouka.

00:16:29.556 --> 00:16:34.561
Shouka Bike-Pushing Championship, Round 2.

00:16:37.697 --> 00:16:42.702
I've decided to call this road Nakamoto Road.

00:16:42.702 --> 00:16:47.707
That way, nobody will take the wrong turn again.

00:17:06.993 --> 00:17:11.998
Nature never lies. Put on sunscreen, and the bees come right over.

00:17:34.788 --> 00:17:39.793
A dried-up snake.

00:17:48.868 --> 00:17:53.873
Honestly, Nakamoto Road isn't that hard to ride.

00:18:17.197 --> 00:18:20.467
You're not cheering anyone on either, you know.

00:19:34.341 --> 00:19:39.346
Sitting on the drainage ditch is just right.

00:19:48.755 --> 00:19:53.760
Built-in stretching board.

00:19:55.462 --> 00:20:00.467
Signal is back. Time to post a story.

00:20:07.273 --> 00:20:12.278
This is probably going to be my lunch.

00:20:38.338 --> 00:20:43.343
I finally see civilization.

00:20:48.948 --> 00:20:53.953
I've never been this excited to see asphalt.

00:20:56.489 --> 00:21:01.494
I probably should've knelt down and licked the road.

00:21:39.766 --> 00:21:44.771
Maybe I should've come here for lunch earlier.

00:21:49.743 --> 00:21:54.748
⚠ Large vehicles often use Route 199, and the road surface here is rough.

00:22:39.125 --> 00:22:44.130
Suddenly, I'm speechless.

00:22:46.666 --> 00:22:51.671
Maybe I should make some sound after all.

00:22:59.979 --> 00:23:04.984
A highlight moment in my cycling life.

00:23:06.686 --> 00:23:10.557
Round-island Shouka checkpoint unlocked.

00:23:11.224 --> 00:23:13.693
Phone camera combo, rapid-fire mode.

00:23:13.693 --> 00:23:18.698
The small wish I made after last year's east coast folding-bike camping trip came true.

00:23:24.270 --> 00:23:29.275
Shouka Bike-Pushing Championship: finished!

00:23:41.154 --> 00:23:46.159
I never thought this day would come.

00:23:46.159 --> 00:23:49.929
Unlocked Shouka by bikepacking.

00:23:49.929 --> 00:23:54.934
It feels like crossing the finish line of a marathon. I can't believe I did it.

00:25:07.874 --> 00:25:12.879
County Road 199 merges onto Provincial Highway 9E.

00:25:24.491 --> 00:25:32.065
After surviving the 8.63% Xuhai Grassland descent,
the downhill feels much more under control.

00:25:39.939 --> 00:25:44.944
Bikepacking weight distribution really does help.

00:26:29.789 --> 00:26:34.794
A cat disguised as public art.

00:27:15.201 --> 00:27:20.206
Monday means fewer people and fewer cars. Much safer to ride.

00:27:43.596 --> 00:27:50.670
⚠ Watch the road conditions.

00:27:53.006 --> 00:27:57.811
⚠ Watch the road conditions.

00:28:02.415 --> 00:28:07.420
Successfully crossed the Central Mountain Range.

00:28:10.690 --> 00:28:15.695
Seeing the Pacific Ocean again.

00:28:36.549 --> 00:28:41.554
The last convenience store I saw was the 7-Eleven in Manzhou.

00:29:56.830 --> 00:30:01.835
Oops. A 30-minute break was way too long.

00:30:23.723 --> 00:30:28.728
I rested too long back there.

00:30:28.728 --> 00:30:33.733
From now on, I need to plan breaks around sunset too.

00:31:07.534 --> 00:31:12.539
The sound of heavy traffic is back. Time to readjust.

00:31:13.606 --> 00:31:18.611
For two days, I'd gotten used to insects and birds instead.

00:31:46.706 --> 00:31:51.711
Withdrawing cash and figuring out dinner.

00:31:56.016 --> 00:32:01.021
Decision made: Ba Kou Fu Omurice.

00:32:58.211 --> 00:33:01.281
Cyclists from Indonesia and the UK.

00:33:33.513 --> 00:33:38.518
Checking out my gear.

00:33:45.658 --> 00:33:50.663
I started this trip from Fangliao by train.

00:33:53.433 --> 00:33:57.303
They rode from Tainan to Fangliao, then on to Kenting.

00:33:59.072 --> 00:34:04.077
Their route is Fangliao, Kenting, then Dawu too.

00:34:06.546 --> 00:34:11.551
Kenting?

00:34:15.321 --> 00:34:20.326
They even went swimming at Baisha Bay.

00:34:32.038 --> 00:34:37.043
The girl even says “itadakimasu.”

00:34:41.748 --> 00:34:46.753
A NT$130 omurice with a generous portion.

00:35:06.840 --> 00:35:11.845
It's actually pretty tasty.

00:35:13.646 --> 00:35:18.651
I'll come back for this next time.

00:35:37.370 --> 00:35:42.375
Time to restock.

00:35:58.458 --> 00:36:03.463
Back to the familiar old spot from a year ago.

00:36:30.590 --> 00:36:35.595
Same time as last year, but with a different ride.

00:36:46.840 --> 00:36:51.845
A short day, but incredibly fulfilling.

00:37:03.156 --> 00:37:08.161
Checking in to let everyone know I'm safe.

00:37:51.538 --> 00:37:56.543
Set up late, pack up early. Time for a shower.

00:38:07.454 --> 00:38:12.459
I can't believe I also fulfilled my quiet wish to conquer Shouka.

00:38:56.536 --> 00:39:01.541
I didn't expect something to happen in the middle of the night.

00:39:02.008 --> 00:39:07.013
A drunk local wanted to try riding my bike.

00:39:19.459 --> 00:39:24.464
He was seriously drunk.

00:39:36.876 --> 00:39:41.881
In the end, without getting my permission,

00:39:41.881 --> 00:39:46.886
he just got on and rode my bike.

00:39:46.886 --> 00:39:51.891
Even though it was only a short distance,

00:39:51.891 --> 00:39:55.528
it really didn't feel okay.

00:39:58.531 --> 00:40:03.536
⚠ So if you're wild camping by bike, remember to lock it.

00:40:06.106 --> 00:40:11.111
A drunk person really might ride your bike away.

00:40:11.111 --> 00:40:14.581
He just kept pestering me.

00:40:16.249 --> 00:40:21.254
I never even lit this candle lantern.

00:40:23.356 --> 00:40:28.361
It's something I wanted, not something I needed. I won't bring it next time.

00:40:44.944 --> 00:40:49.949
The happiest thing today was unlocking Shouka.

00:40:51.284 --> 00:40:56.289
A small wish from last year.

00:40:56.456 --> 00:41:01.461
Changed the bike, upgraded it, trained for it.

00:41:02.328 --> 00:41:07.333
Step by step, I made my own dream happen.

00:41:08.802 --> 00:41:15.842
Just like back then, sitting in the office,
suddenly wanting to challenge a motorcycle trip around Taiwan.

00:41:16.743 --> 00:41:21.748
Cycling makes you feel 10 years younger. Pitching a tent makes you feel 10 years younger too.

00:41:22.215 --> 00:41:27.220
Cycling cures everything.

00:41:27.721 --> 00:41:32.726
Outdoor adventures always brighten the mood.

